WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.144 --> 00:00:03.977
- What's up believe nation?

00:00:03.977 --> 00:00:04.810
It's Evan.

00:00:04.810 --> 00:00:05.892
My one word is believe.

00:00:05.892 --> 00:00:07.775
And I believe in people
more than they believe

00:00:07.775 --> 00:00:11.013
in themselves and my sincere
hope is that if you see

00:00:11.013 --> 00:00:14.129
in you, what I see in you, you'll be able

00:00:14.129 --> 00:00:15.572
to change the planet.

00:00:15.572 --> 00:00:16.899
So to help you on your journey today,

00:00:16.899 --> 00:00:19.104
I'm going to talk about
the seven ways to discover

00:00:19.104 --> 00:00:21.405
your strengths and weaknesses.

00:00:21.405 --> 00:00:24.655
- [Introductory Music] Nine, eight, go.

00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:30.621
- So the question I get
asked a lot by different

00:00:30.621 --> 00:00:32.475
entrepreneurs trying to
figure out their path,

00:00:32.475 --> 00:00:33.647
figure out where they're going to go is,

00:00:33.647 --> 00:00:35.841
"What am I good at? What am I
strong at? What am I weak at?

00:00:35.841 --> 00:00:39.027
"And how do I use that to
build a successful business?"

00:00:39.027 --> 00:00:41.811
So today I'm going to share
with you my seven tips

00:00:41.811 --> 00:00:45.894
on how to discover your
strengths and weaknesses.

00:00:47.833 --> 00:00:50.080
Tip number one is just
think about what do you

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:51.768
have the most fun doing?

00:00:51.768 --> 00:00:53.311
A lot of times we get too in our head,

00:00:53.311 --> 00:00:56.115
we're too analytical,
we're too data-oriented,

00:00:56.115 --> 00:00:59.033
we're too process-oriented and
an easy way to step out of it

00:00:59.033 --> 00:01:00.592
is to just think, "What do I enjoy doing?

00:01:00.592 --> 00:01:01.715
"What do I have the most fun doing?

00:01:01.715 --> 00:01:03.374
"What do I get lost in?"

00:01:03.374 --> 00:01:05.841
We all have something
that we can get lost in.

00:01:05.841 --> 00:01:07.875
And now it is there's no stupid answers

00:01:07.875 --> 00:01:11.166
'cause you could turn almost
anything into a career.

00:01:11.166 --> 00:01:13.116
You know, 10 years ago, if
you said that you wanted

00:01:13.116 --> 00:01:16.155
to be a gamer, that
wouldn't have worked out.

00:01:16.155 --> 00:01:17.745
You wouldn't have been able to make money

00:01:17.745 --> 00:01:19.473
as a professional gamer but now,

00:01:19.473 --> 00:01:21.563
a lot of professional
gamers are making more than

00:01:21.563 --> 00:01:22.982
our parents made right?

00:01:22.982 --> 00:01:26.331
If you're a faker, or if
you're a double lift or

00:01:26.331 --> 00:01:28.271
if you're in the legal legend
scene or the other games

00:01:28.271 --> 00:01:31.067
as well, like you're making some money.

00:01:31.067 --> 00:01:32.504
And that is doable.

00:01:32.504 --> 00:01:33.337
Another option.

00:01:33.337 --> 00:01:34.418
If you like hanging out with your friends.

00:01:34.418 --> 00:01:36.288
If you're really people-oriented person,

00:01:36.288 --> 00:01:37.398
that's a strong strength.

00:01:37.398 --> 00:01:41.891
That my lead you to a
career in HR or a business

00:01:41.891 --> 00:01:44.616
as a speaker or a business
as a coach or consultant

00:01:44.616 --> 00:01:45.671
with other people.

00:01:45.671 --> 00:01:48.322
So just think about before
trying to figure out

00:01:48.322 --> 00:01:50.090
how it's all going to make sense,

00:01:50.090 --> 00:01:51.532
that's what we always get caught up.

00:01:51.532 --> 00:01:54.071
Before thinking about how does
this turn into a perfect plan

00:01:54.071 --> 00:01:57.134
for myself, just think about
what can I get lost in?

00:01:57.134 --> 00:01:58.478
What do I love doing?

00:01:58.478 --> 00:02:01.541
If I didn't have
responsibilities, or the great

00:02:01.541 --> 00:02:03.493
question, if I had all
the money in the world,

00:02:03.493 --> 00:02:04.848
what would I do with my time?

00:02:04.848 --> 00:02:05.795
Yes, you're going to travel.

00:02:05.795 --> 00:02:07.406
Yes, you're going to buy whatever.

00:02:07.406 --> 00:02:08.284
You're going to buy all this stuff.

00:02:08.284 --> 00:02:09.117
Great.

00:02:09.117 --> 00:02:09.950
You still have money left over.

00:02:09.950 --> 00:02:11.134
You still have time in abundance.

00:02:11.134 --> 00:02:12.268
What are you going to do?

00:02:12.268 --> 00:02:13.301
'Cause you'll get sick of traveling.

00:02:13.301 --> 00:02:14.471
You'll get sick of buying stuff.

00:02:14.471 --> 00:02:15.962
You'll need to do something
that has a little bit more

00:02:15.962 --> 00:02:16.933
meaning to your life.

00:02:16.933 --> 00:02:19.379
I promise you, you'd be
saying, "No that's not true".

00:02:19.379 --> 00:02:21.045
It's true. It'll happen.

00:02:21.045 --> 00:02:23.322
So what would you do if
you had that kind of money?

00:02:23.322 --> 00:02:24.477
What would you do with your time?

00:02:24.477 --> 00:02:27.020
And thinking about that,
then allows you to think,

00:02:27.020 --> 00:02:28.890
"Then okay, I really like those things".

00:02:28.890 --> 00:02:30.414
From there, you can
pull out your strengths

00:02:30.414 --> 00:02:31.247
and weaknesses.

00:02:31.247 --> 00:02:32.932
Really making lists of the
things that you can get

00:02:32.932 --> 00:02:36.015
lost in and that you just love doing.

00:02:38.148 --> 00:02:40.747
Step number two is think
about what you daydream about.

00:02:40.747 --> 00:02:42.316
So, it may not be what
you're doing right now,

00:02:42.316 --> 00:02:46.096
but when you lie in bed
about to pass out or when you

00:02:46.096 --> 00:02:48.711
are in the shower thinking
or when you're walking

00:02:48.711 --> 00:02:50.624
through nature going on
a hike, or when you're

00:02:50.624 --> 00:02:53.254
traveling or lying on the
beach or whatever it is

00:02:53.254 --> 00:02:55.454
that you kind of get hit
with some inspiration,

00:02:55.454 --> 00:02:57.285
what do you daydream about doing?

00:02:57.285 --> 00:02:58.665
Maybe, you're not doing
it yet, but you wish

00:02:58.665 --> 00:02:59.498
you could do it.

00:02:59.498 --> 00:03:02.379
You have these crazy dreams
sometimes that I wish

00:03:02.379 --> 00:03:05.308
I could be doing that or
people you look up to.

00:03:05.308 --> 00:03:07.396
When you think about
what you daydream about,

00:03:07.396 --> 00:03:10.043
again don't make it practical yet.

00:03:10.043 --> 00:03:12.552
Just write down a list of
things that you wish you

00:03:12.552 --> 00:03:13.736
could be spending your time on.

00:03:13.736 --> 00:03:15.401
You wish you could be doing.

00:03:15.401 --> 00:03:17.632
And then, I would try
to find some small way

00:03:17.632 --> 00:03:18.940
to actually start doing it.

00:03:18.940 --> 00:03:20.428
The test to see if you like it,

00:03:20.428 --> 00:03:21.561
To see if you're good at it.

00:03:21.561 --> 00:03:23.731
A lot of times, the grass is
greener on the other side.

00:03:23.731 --> 00:03:25.820
A lot of times, that
thing that you want to do,

00:03:25.820 --> 00:03:28.889
once you start doing it, is
way too much work and not

00:03:28.889 --> 00:03:30.709
what you thought it was going to be.

00:03:30.709 --> 00:03:32.101
And you don't want to do it anymore.

00:03:32.101 --> 00:03:34.558
But sometimes, when you do
it, it's like, "I love this.

00:03:34.558 --> 00:03:35.897
"I want to keep doing it".

00:03:35.897 --> 00:03:38.373
So, you never know, until you get started.

00:03:38.373 --> 00:03:40.340
I never thought I'd be a salsa dancer.

00:03:40.340 --> 00:03:41.989
I never thought I would
run a salsa school,

00:03:41.989 --> 00:03:43.730
invest and buy it.

00:03:43.730 --> 00:03:45.850
I'd never thought that'd
be part of my plan.

00:03:45.850 --> 00:03:46.960
I'm tall, I didn't speak Spanish.

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:48.052
You know, I take big steps.

00:03:48.052 --> 00:03:49.887
I didn't learn the music growing up.

00:03:49.887 --> 00:03:51.870
It's all on paper, there's
all the reasons why

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:54.819
it would never work out
for me as a salsa dancer

00:03:54.819 --> 00:03:57.300
but I just loved it and I went to a class.

00:03:57.300 --> 00:03:58.133
I wanted to go back.

00:03:58.133 --> 00:03:58.966
I wanted to do it again.

00:03:58.966 --> 00:04:00.091
I wanted to do it again.

00:04:00.091 --> 00:04:01.073
Same thing as YouTube videos.

00:04:01.073 --> 00:04:02.457
My first videos sucked.

00:04:02.457 --> 00:04:03.486
They really were bad.

00:04:03.486 --> 00:04:04.344
But I liked it.

00:04:04.344 --> 00:04:05.226
I liked the process.

00:04:05.226 --> 00:04:06.162
I wanted to do it again.

00:04:06.162 --> 00:04:07.085
And I wanted to do it again.

00:04:07.085 --> 00:04:07.918
I wasn't getting any results.

00:04:07.918 --> 00:04:09.488
I wasn't getting any
comments, no views, no shares,

00:04:09.488 --> 00:04:10.321
nothing.

00:04:10.321 --> 00:04:13.013
I just loved it so I had to do
it again and again and again.

00:04:13.013 --> 00:04:16.135
And so, instead of making
it some big plan on what

00:04:16.135 --> 00:04:17.758
you want to do with your life;

00:04:17.758 --> 00:04:18.875
that can seem overwhelming.

00:04:18.875 --> 00:04:20.077
That can seem depressing.

00:04:20.077 --> 00:04:22.236
It's upsetting because
you don't have clarity.

00:04:22.236 --> 00:04:23.374
I would just think about the things

00:04:23.374 --> 00:04:25.362
that you have some daydreams about.

00:04:25.362 --> 00:04:26.824
That you wish you could do and then find,

00:04:26.824 --> 00:04:29.399
some small way to get started.

00:04:29.399 --> 00:04:31.107
Just hit that little bit of the pyramid

00:04:31.107 --> 00:04:33.119
instead of just thinking
about it as this huge project,

00:04:33.119 --> 00:04:34.711
just this little thin wedge,

00:04:34.711 --> 00:04:37.082
this little tiny piece to test it.

00:04:37.082 --> 00:04:38.945
To say "yes" to one thing.

00:04:38.945 --> 00:04:40.942
You could say "yes" to
going to try rock climbing

00:04:40.942 --> 00:04:43.381
without having to become a
professional rock climber.

00:04:43.381 --> 00:04:44.938
You could say "yes" to going out on a date

00:04:44.938 --> 00:04:46.319
with one girl to see how it works out,

00:04:46.319 --> 00:04:47.915
without having to get married to her.

00:04:47.915 --> 00:04:48.748
Right?

00:04:48.748 --> 00:04:50.222
So say "yes". Try it.

00:04:50.222 --> 00:04:51.351
The thing you have in your
mind, find some small way

00:04:51.351 --> 00:04:52.566
to get started.

00:04:52.566 --> 00:04:53.873
And then you'll see if you enjoy it

00:04:53.873 --> 00:04:56.456
and if your strengths come out.

00:04:58.882 --> 00:05:00.593
Tip number three is think
about what do you do

00:05:00.593 --> 00:05:02.065
differently than others?

00:05:02.065 --> 00:05:05.020
You are a strange duck in some respects.

00:05:05.020 --> 00:05:06.894
You are not exactly like everybody else.

00:05:06.894 --> 00:05:08.636
You're not the same as
all your other friends.

00:05:08.636 --> 00:05:10.648
You are your own unique little snowflake.

00:05:10.648 --> 00:05:14.069
And so, what is it that you
do or the way that you think

00:05:14.069 --> 00:05:16.589
that is just different than other people?

00:05:16.589 --> 00:05:18.113
It's an important question to ask because

00:05:18.113 --> 00:05:20.990
a lot of times you may not
see those things as strengths,

00:05:20.990 --> 00:05:23.832
you may even see those
things as weaknesses.

00:05:23.832 --> 00:05:26.080
That because you're
different, you're not good

00:05:26.080 --> 00:05:28.564
like the other people
are at this other thing.

00:05:28.564 --> 00:05:30.936
But you see the world slightly differently

00:05:30.936 --> 00:05:32.458
than other people do.

00:05:32.458 --> 00:05:34.954
And where do you stand
out compared to the people

00:05:34.954 --> 00:05:35.981
around you?

00:05:35.981 --> 00:05:37.741
And just asking that
question, will pull out

00:05:37.741 --> 00:05:40.818
some things that are very interesting.

00:05:40.818 --> 00:05:43.818
So, for me, I'm very mission-driven.

00:05:44.874 --> 00:05:47.197
I'm also very pragmatic.

00:05:47.197 --> 00:05:51.274
I don't really hang out a lot
of times just going for beer,

00:05:51.274 --> 00:05:53.286
and watching movies with friends.

00:05:53.286 --> 00:05:55.607
A lot of times, there's a
purpose behind what I do.

00:05:55.607 --> 00:05:58.811
There's a purpose behind
the conversations I have.

00:05:58.811 --> 00:06:00.452
I don't like dealing with small problems.

00:06:00.452 --> 00:06:03.621
I want to look behind it
to see the bigger cause

00:06:03.621 --> 00:06:05.744
and go out and solve that big thing.

00:06:05.744 --> 00:06:08.269
That could be a weakness
in some social settings

00:06:08.269 --> 00:06:10.350
but it's also a strength
for me in that it allows me

00:06:10.350 --> 00:06:11.683
to build this business.

00:06:11.683 --> 00:06:12.730
It allows me to build this movement.

00:06:12.730 --> 00:06:14.852
It allows me to create great content

00:06:14.852 --> 00:06:16.612
and videos for you guys.

00:06:16.612 --> 00:06:19.520
And so just asking yourself,
what do I do that's different

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:20.650
than most people?

00:06:20.650 --> 00:06:22.688
Again, without thinking
about how it's going to apply

00:06:22.688 --> 00:06:23.852
practically down the road,

00:06:23.852 --> 00:06:25.532
just what do I do that's different?

00:06:25.532 --> 00:06:28.111
Or what do I think
about in a different way

00:06:28.111 --> 00:06:29.521
than the people around me?

00:06:29.521 --> 00:06:31.416
And make a list and though
there you'll be able to find

00:06:31.416 --> 00:06:33.963
some of the what you might
have thought were weaknesses

00:06:33.963 --> 00:06:38.130
but could actually be strengths
for your future career.

00:06:39.858 --> 00:06:44.025
- So tip number four is be
brutally honest with yourself.

00:06:44.947 --> 00:06:48.062
All of us are so unique and
we have different strengths

00:06:48.062 --> 00:06:49.598
and weaknesses.

00:06:49.598 --> 00:06:53.839
And sometimes, admitting to
some of them could be really

00:06:53.839 --> 00:06:56.143
embarrassing for us.

00:06:56.143 --> 00:07:00.546
So for example, I'm an
organizational disaster.

00:07:00.546 --> 00:07:03.467
I don't do well with organization at all.

00:07:03.467 --> 00:07:07.812
Which is why I have to create
structure around my life.

00:07:07.812 --> 00:07:10.963
I have to schedule my
days to do specific things

00:07:10.963 --> 00:07:13.624
because if I don't, I'm
going to fall off track

00:07:13.624 --> 00:07:16.675
and I'll just find
myself lying on the floor

00:07:16.675 --> 00:07:19.067
staring at the ceilings, dreaming about

00:07:19.067 --> 00:07:20.672
a brighter future.

00:07:20.672 --> 00:07:23.707
The truth is that brighter
future will never come

00:07:23.707 --> 00:07:26.901
if I don't do something
about my organization.

00:07:26.901 --> 00:07:30.471
That's why I stick to my
schedule as much as possible

00:07:30.471 --> 00:07:33.627
and I only stray away from
it when there's something

00:07:33.627 --> 00:07:35.911
urgent that needs to be taken care of.

00:07:35.911 --> 00:07:38.896
And on the other side,
I did not want to admit

00:07:38.896 --> 00:07:41.113
that my strength is empathy.

00:07:41.113 --> 00:07:44.568
Especially when I started
out in the workforce

00:07:44.568 --> 00:07:47.733
and I was up against all these alpha-males

00:07:47.733 --> 00:07:50.796
and they're like, "Oh,
you're such as woman.

00:07:50.796 --> 00:07:54.375
"You just want to hold hands
and hug people and feel

00:07:54.375 --> 00:07:55.378
"where people are feeling".

00:07:55.378 --> 00:07:57.879
And I hid it inside of me for a long time.

00:07:57.879 --> 00:08:02.200
And I took on personas
that wasn't even mine.

00:08:02.200 --> 00:08:05.518
And then eventually, I admitted to myself.

00:08:05.518 --> 00:08:09.227
Empathy is not only a strength
for me, it's my super power.

00:08:09.227 --> 00:08:13.394
It allows me to feel what
other people are feeling.

00:08:14.819 --> 00:08:16.762
My mission is to help people.

00:08:16.762 --> 00:08:18.991
What better way to help people

00:08:18.991 --> 00:08:20.698
than feel what they're feeling

00:08:20.698 --> 00:08:24.705
and really understand what
they're going through?

00:08:24.705 --> 00:08:27.558
I think most of us are
aware of our strengths

00:08:27.558 --> 00:08:29.047
and weaknesses.

00:08:29.047 --> 00:08:32.869
The only thing you need
to do is just be brutally

00:08:32.869 --> 00:08:34.619
honest with yourself.

00:08:37.817 --> 00:08:40.068
- Number five is use your
friends as counselors

00:08:40.068 --> 00:08:41.201
but not jailers.

00:08:41.201 --> 00:08:43.157
So one of the things we tend
to do when we don't know

00:08:43.157 --> 00:08:45.633
the answer to something,
is we ask our friends.

00:08:45.633 --> 00:08:47.622
And our friends can be a great window

00:08:47.622 --> 00:08:49.862
into understanding us a little bit better.

00:08:49.862 --> 00:08:51.981
Asking your friend what
you think your strengths

00:08:51.981 --> 00:08:54.352
and weaknesses are can
give you a perspective

00:08:54.352 --> 00:08:55.421
on yourself.

00:08:55.421 --> 00:08:57.407
The thing is though, you
have to be careful about it.

00:08:57.407 --> 00:09:00.251
Because your friends see one side of you.

00:09:00.251 --> 00:09:02.842
They see a certain side
that maybe one friend

00:09:02.842 --> 00:09:05.004
sees one side, another
friend sees another side,

00:09:05.004 --> 00:09:07.544
and there's still a piece
of you too that's hidden,

00:09:07.544 --> 00:09:08.582
that you haven't shared with anybody,

00:09:08.582 --> 00:09:10.633
that you just keep to yourself,

00:09:10.633 --> 00:09:12.481
that you don't want exposed.

00:09:12.481 --> 00:09:15.148
And so, the positive
of asking your friends

00:09:15.148 --> 00:09:16.495
what you think you're
strengths and weaknesses are

00:09:16.495 --> 00:09:18.498
is that you get some insight into you

00:09:18.498 --> 00:09:20.350
and to that side that you are showing.

00:09:20.350 --> 00:09:22.693
The negative side though
is that because they only

00:09:22.693 --> 00:09:27.088
see one aspect of you, that
that becomes your jail cell.

00:09:27.088 --> 00:09:29.133
That because this is how they see you,

00:09:29.133 --> 00:09:31.201
you have to continue
behaving only in that way

00:09:31.201 --> 00:09:33.525
and going on those strengths
and you're missing this

00:09:33.525 --> 00:09:35.619
whole other part that you're not sharing.

00:09:35.619 --> 00:09:39.192
And so, I'm always
reluctant on any of these

00:09:39.192 --> 00:09:42.719
personal development
exercises and self-awareness,

00:09:42.719 --> 00:09:43.566
because that is what it is.

00:09:43.566 --> 00:09:45.274
It's your self-awareness.

00:09:45.274 --> 00:09:47.106
I'm always reluctant to go outside

00:09:47.106 --> 00:09:48.787
and ask other people.

00:09:48.787 --> 00:09:51.483
I think your time is
better spent with yourself.

00:09:51.483 --> 00:09:54.426
Spend more time with yourself
than time with other people

00:09:54.426 --> 00:09:56.142
if you want to understand yourself

00:09:56.142 --> 00:09:59.959
because the answers are
here, not out there.

00:09:59.959 --> 00:10:04.012
But if you want to, it
gives you a perspective.

00:10:04.012 --> 00:10:06.502
So again, use your friends as counselors

00:10:06.502 --> 00:10:07.335
but not as jailers.

00:10:07.335 --> 00:10:09.393
You don't have to live
up to their expectations

00:10:09.393 --> 00:10:11.052
or that one side of you

00:10:11.052 --> 00:10:12.408
and spending some good time with yourself

00:10:12.408 --> 00:10:15.327
to reflect, to write down,
to spend time in nature,

00:10:15.327 --> 00:10:17.957
to think about the whole you and

00:10:17.957 --> 00:10:20.105
what you're really good at
and where you want to focus

00:10:20.105 --> 00:10:21.188
is important.

00:10:24.025 --> 00:10:27.026
Tip number six is ask yourself
what do you hate doing?

00:10:27.026 --> 00:10:29.182
Often the way to find what you're good at,

00:10:29.182 --> 00:10:31.249
is by thinking about
what you're not good at.

00:10:31.249 --> 00:10:33.399
So just like in the
process of your one word,

00:10:33.399 --> 00:10:35.420
some people find it easier
to find their one word,

00:10:35.420 --> 00:10:36.852
their one most important core value,

00:10:36.852 --> 00:10:38.413
by going positive,
thinking about all the good

00:10:38.413 --> 00:10:39.353
things in their life

00:10:39.353 --> 00:10:40.678
and figuring out what their most important

00:10:40.678 --> 00:10:42.287
core value is.

00:10:42.287 --> 00:10:45.404
Some people can't get down
to it only going positive.

00:10:45.404 --> 00:10:48.104
They find it better going
opposite, going negative.

00:10:48.104 --> 00:10:49.613
So think about the people
who you can't stand

00:10:49.613 --> 00:10:50.536
being around.

00:10:50.536 --> 00:10:52.211
What values do they have?

00:10:52.211 --> 00:10:53.635
What's just like toxic to you?

00:10:53.635 --> 00:10:55.878
You can't stand being around
these kinds of people.

00:10:55.878 --> 00:10:57.834
Or being in these kinds of situations.

00:10:57.834 --> 00:11:00.080
And by figuring out that,
that's your anti-word,

00:11:00.080 --> 00:11:01.941
you can figure out your one word.

00:11:01.941 --> 00:11:04.577
And so think about what you hate doing.

00:11:04.577 --> 00:11:07.020
Think about what other
people may like doing,

00:11:07.020 --> 00:11:08.180
the people around you, they enjoy doing

00:11:08.180 --> 00:11:10.106
but for you it's like, "I can't believe

00:11:10.106 --> 00:11:11.206
"people like doing that".

00:11:11.206 --> 00:11:14.233
What would you absolutely
hate spending your time on

00:11:14.233 --> 00:11:15.795
every single day?

00:11:15.795 --> 00:11:17.879
And that gets you to a list of weaknesses

00:11:17.879 --> 00:11:20.201
and the opposite will be
what you're really good at.

00:11:20.201 --> 00:11:22.679
So what is the thing that
you absolutely hate doing

00:11:22.679 --> 00:11:24.507
and then what's the
exact opposite of that?

00:11:24.507 --> 00:11:28.507
Chances are, that's where
you should be playing.

00:11:30.251 --> 00:11:32.957
And tip number seven
is just say "Yes" more.

00:11:32.957 --> 00:11:34.827
If you have no idea what your passion is,

00:11:34.827 --> 00:11:36.332
If you have no idea what your strengths

00:11:36.332 --> 00:11:38.672
and your weaknesses are,
just say "yes" more.

00:11:38.672 --> 00:11:40.320
When someboody invites
you to do something,

00:11:40.320 --> 00:11:42.100
don't immediately judge it and say,

00:11:42.100 --> 00:11:44.184
"Well this is not going to be for me".

00:11:44.184 --> 00:11:46.504
Say "yes". Try it. See
if you want to go back.

00:11:46.504 --> 00:11:47.465
See if you want to do it again.

00:11:47.465 --> 00:11:49.359
See if it sparked anything.

00:11:49.359 --> 00:11:51.497
We talked about not putting
up so much pressure on it

00:11:51.497 --> 00:11:52.619
being the perfect thing

00:11:52.619 --> 00:11:54.772
and making it some big,
huge project and it has to

00:11:54.772 --> 00:11:55.605
work out.

00:11:55.605 --> 00:11:58.454
But also just exposing
yourself to more things,

00:11:58.454 --> 00:11:59.763
exposing yourself to opportunities

00:11:59.763 --> 00:12:01.940
that maybe your parents
wouldn't agree with

00:12:01.940 --> 00:12:03.505
or maybe it wasn't a part of your culture,

00:12:03.505 --> 00:12:05.404
but it's still kind of curious for you.

00:12:05.404 --> 00:12:07.186
If something hits on your radar and say,

00:12:07.186 --> 00:12:09.193
"Hmm, that's interesting"
or a friend comes

00:12:09.193 --> 00:12:11.938
and tells you, "I want you
to come out to this thing",

00:12:11.938 --> 00:12:13.162
at least try it once.

00:12:13.162 --> 00:12:15.610
It's good to adopt the mentality of to try

00:12:15.610 --> 00:12:16.600
almost anything.

00:12:16.600 --> 00:12:17.761
You know within reason.

00:12:17.761 --> 00:12:18.684
Once.

00:12:18.684 --> 00:12:19.691
Try new foods once.

00:12:19.691 --> 00:12:20.763
Try a new club once.

00:12:20.763 --> 00:12:21.964
Try a new activity once.

00:12:21.964 --> 00:12:23.445
Try a new kind of movie once.

00:12:23.445 --> 00:12:25.851
If you've tried it and it
doesn't work out, great.

00:12:25.851 --> 00:12:27.760
You know, you don't have to do it again.

00:12:27.760 --> 00:12:29.591
But at least, trying it once.

00:12:29.591 --> 00:12:32.380
Because I think most of the
time we discount so many things

00:12:32.380 --> 00:12:33.592
that we've never even tried.

00:12:33.592 --> 00:12:36.399
We're judging things
we've never even spent

00:12:36.399 --> 00:12:37.875
any amount of time on

00:12:37.875 --> 00:12:40.654
and then you just constantly
live in this narrow lane.

00:12:40.654 --> 00:12:42.248
And that's probably not
even the best path for you.

00:12:42.248 --> 00:12:44.796
There's some path way out
here that you don't even

00:12:44.796 --> 00:12:47.170
know you should be on
because you never bothered

00:12:47.170 --> 00:12:48.492
expanding your horizon.

00:12:48.492 --> 00:12:50.585
So if you feel lost, if you
feel like you don't know

00:12:50.585 --> 00:12:52.392
what you're strengths
and your weaknesses are,

00:12:52.392 --> 00:12:54.446
if you like you don't know
what you're passionate about,

00:12:54.446 --> 00:12:57.543
then try multiple things
at least once say "yes"

00:12:57.543 --> 00:12:59.702
to a lot of things and if
it doesn't work, great.

00:12:59.702 --> 00:13:00.535
Kill it.

00:13:00.535 --> 00:13:01.671
You don't have to make
a lifelong commitment

00:13:01.671 --> 00:13:03.615
to being a salsa dancer.

00:13:03.615 --> 00:13:04.987
If you go to a class, you don't like it,

00:13:04.987 --> 00:13:06.423
but at least say "yes" once.

00:13:06.423 --> 00:13:07.256
Try it.

00:13:07.256 --> 00:13:08.089
See if it's for you.

00:13:08.089 --> 00:13:08.922
See if you want to go back.

00:13:08.922 --> 00:13:12.019
Expand that reach, say "yes"
once to almost anything

00:13:12.019 --> 00:13:14.185
and through that process,
you'll discover your passion,

00:13:14.185 --> 00:13:16.386
your strengths and your weaknesses.

00:13:16.386 --> 00:13:17.696
So those are my seven
tips on how to discover

00:13:17.696 --> 00:13:18.862
your strengths and weaknesses.

